# ASCII-First -- plain ASCII for documents and commits

**Seated:** `20260816.214652` on Keaton's word. Canonical twin: `.claude/rules/ascii-first.md` (full form). Kin: `reds-first.mdc`, REDS %83.

Write every new document, code comment, and commit message in **plain 7-bit ASCII**. A non-ASCII character no reader needs is a corruption waiting to compound -- ITINERARY.md silently triple-encoded into 2,797 runs of mojibake before it was caught (REDS %83).

Substitute: em/en-dash -> `--`/`-`; middot -> `-`/`,`/`;`; curly quotes -> straight `'`/`"`; arrows -> `->`/`<-`/`<->`; ellipsis -> `...`; typographic minus (U+2212) -> `-`; Greek/subscripts in prose -> spelled (`gamma_2`, `sigma`).

**Exception:** an explicitly-named set of work rounds where non-ASCII is the point (a Unicode module's fixtures, an i18n surface, a font codec's glyph tables). Name it in the round; keep it out of the operator card, commit subjects, and general prose.

**Eight guards stand**, all rostered in `construction/standing-equipment.kyri`: `living_card_ascii` (the operator card and the ledger, plus valid UTF-8 across every tracked text file), `ascii_document` (the rule rooms gated at zero, every other living `.md` on a falling ceiling), `ascii_comment` (Rye, shell and Rishi, Glow), `spoken_ascii` (what a Rishi guard says out loud -- the fourth subject, which the sentence above does not name), `rye_spoken_ascii` (what a **Rye** program prints, seated `20260908.214712` -- the same subject in the language this tree writes most of its own modules in, read by parenthesis depth because half of it sits on a `++` continuation line), and `rye_written_ascii` (what a Rye program ASSEMBLES into a buffer and hands onward, seated `20260911.215028` -- a `bufPrint`, `bufPrintZ`, `allocPrint` or `writeFile` region, since every meter before it read what a source comments or what a program prints and none read what it writes, which is the surface REDS %83 actually happened on; a ratchet over all 290 assembled characters and a WALL at zero over the two that reached a disk, both repaired on its seating lap), `shell_written_ascii` (what a SHELL program assembles in a heredoc and feeds onward, seated `20260912.023000` -- the Rye meter's own half one language over, whose header priced the shell residue at two characters from the two fixtures it could see while the real population read 1,419 across 122 files; it classifies the subset a bare interpreter consumes as code apart from the data a script feeds onward, so a lane acts on `sweepable` rather than on the total), and `shell_emit_ascii` (what a POSIX shell script SPEAKS through `echo` or `printf`, seated `20260916.183114` -- the operand region found by a quote walk, since a `#` inside a string does not end the line and a `>` inside a quoted argument is prose rather than a redirect; the fifth meter named `printf` as its gap and the population was `echo` by three to one, because a `.sh` file has no `say` verb and the spoken meter opens `.rish` alone, leaving that whole surface outside the family by construction). Full form and current readings: the Claude twin.

**Never rewrite dated artifacts** to retrofit this (one-clock law, accrete-never-break); repairing a mojibake *corruption* is a fix, not a style rewrite.
